WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
Please welcome Nicola Coughlan.

2
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.564
Nicola!

3
00:00:04.564 --> 00:00:06.895
(audience applauding)

4
00:00:06.895 --> 00:00:09.750
Okay, look at you.

5
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:10.583
Oh my God!

6
00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:12.642
You look so Traci.

7
00:00:12.642 --> 00:00:14.421
Hug, hug, hug, hug.

8
00:00:14.421 --> 00:00:15.599
Oh my gosh!

9
00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:18.766
(audience applauding)

10
00:00:21.498 --> 00:00:23.661
Oh my gosh.

11
00:00:23.661 --> 00:00:24.494
Hi!

12
00:00:24.494 --> 00:00:27.473
Have you seen any of our obsession with yourselves?

13
00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:28.730
I absolutely have.

14
00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.190
I was right on top of all of it.

15
00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.450
I was honored and delighted.

16
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:32.360 line:15%
It was amazing.

17
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.210 line:15%
It was just so surreal

18
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.470 line:15%
because it all happened in December, 2020

19
00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.820 line:15%
when we were all locked in our houses.

20
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.467 line:15%
And I was like, "How have they seen the show?"

21
00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.660
"How do they know who we are?"

22
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.539
It was mind blowing.

23
00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:43.190
Everybody watches the show.

24
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.530
I mean, it changed lives.

25
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:49.040
Now, I don't wanna be a spoiler.

26
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.030
So, if you don't want any spoiler alerts, cover your ears.

27
00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.160
One, two, three.

28
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.210
Your character has been revealed-

29
00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.930
Yes.
As none other than the one.

30
00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:00.350
Lady Whistledown!

31
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.998
It's you?
It is.

32
00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:03.000
Yes, I know.
Okay.

33
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.370
I was screaming at the TV.

34
00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:10.010
Of course, this is like the gossip columnist of the town.

35
00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.780
All season one, we're trying to figure out who it is.

36
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.613
It's you!

37
00:01:12.613 --> 00:01:14.700
I know, it was crazy because they were not sure

38
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.140
whether they were gonna reveal it or not.

39
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.190
It was sort of a debate

40
00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.170 line:15%
but then what you see in season two,

41
00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.750 line:15%
you can see why they revealed at the end of season one.

42
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:23.838 line:15%
That's a tease.

43
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:25.170 line:15%
Okay.
And you know,

44
00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.230
you are pulling the puppet strings to so much of the show.

45
00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.063
Yeah.

46
00:01:30.063 --> 00:01:34.253
And not until the last second 82 million people were like,

47
00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.263
I know.

48
00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:38.830
How did you keep the mystery knowing...

49
00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.410
I did not keep it well, unsaid in any way, shape or form.

50
00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.243
Really?
I was like,

51
00:01:42.243 --> 00:01:43.277
I would go to people like during lunch break,

52
00:01:43.277 --> 00:01:44.530
"Do you know who Lady Whistledown in is?"

53
00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.170
They were like, "No", I was like, "It's me, it is me"

54
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.360
So, that's how I sort of tempered it

55
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.730
without telling the rest of the world.

56
00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.610
I was very good at just telling people on set

57
00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.443
that it was me.

58
00:01:52.443 --> 00:01:53.440
And it was crazy

59
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.860
because it was such a huge secret to keep

60
00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.110
even doing press for season one,

61
00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.110
they're "Lady Whistledown", I was like...

62
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.020
What about your friends?

63
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.670
We're like, "Look me in the eye, is it you?"

64
00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.370
I did tell a lot of them and they were so mad at me.

65
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.360
So this season I've been not allowed to tell them anything.

66
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.220
They don't wanna know anything about it.

67
00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.590
I watched a little bit with my mom already.

68
00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.820
And they were turning around at me, going...

69
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.297
And I was like, "I know, didn't I do good secret keeping?"

70
00:02:17.297 --> 00:02:20.510
"Am I not better at that than thought I was?"

71
00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:24.810
And it's not like easy becoming Penelope.

72
00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.300
At sometimes there's real transformations-

73
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.120
Oh yes.
Especially in period.

74
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:29.953
Oh yeah.

75
00:02:29.953 --> 00:02:30.786
And look at this time lapse video.

76
00:02:30.786 --> 00:02:31.720
Yeah.
I just love this.

77
00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.205
In my Hamilton sweatshirt with a puppy on my knee.

78
00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:35.390
Aww!

79
00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:36.830
So every day you're going through...

80
00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.320
And this takes hours, right?

81
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.680
This takes about three hours.

82
00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.110
I can say, yeah.

83
00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.280
So, it's like a big transformation

84
00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.240
and that wig is made, you know, hair by hair,

85
00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.590
like it's all really intricate,

86
00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.510
all the colors, like they're matched up.

87
00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.270
There's so much thought that goes in.

88
00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.490
Didn't you have a teacher tell you

89
00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:52.761
that you would never

90
00:02:52.761 --> 00:02:54.870
Do a period piece?
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

91
00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.400
They also told me I didn't look Irish

92
00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.900
which I don't know what that means.

93
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.733
Because you're Irish.

94
00:02:58.733 --> 00:02:59.730
They were like, "You do not look Irish."

95
00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:03.077 line:15%
I was like, "Okay, I will do I wear a wooly jumper"

96
00:03:03.077 --> 00:03:05.280 line:15%
"and carry some shamrocks and then..."

97
00:03:06.412 --> 00:03:07.245 line:15%
I dunno.

98
00:03:07.245 --> 00:03:08.780 line:15%
Yeah, they said to me, you'll never do period.

99
00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.613
And I was like, "Okay."

100
00:03:09.613 --> 00:03:11.940
And at drama school you're like a little sponge.

101
00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.240
You'll take everything a teacher says.

102
00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:14.600
You'd be like, "Sure, sure, sure."

103
00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.433
So I would tell people like,

104
00:03:15.433 --> 00:03:17.150
"Well, I'll never do period drama."

105
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.630
They said, yeah, "My face was too modern."

106
00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:20.880
Live your life.
Absolutely.

107
00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.300
I'd like to tell him he was wrong

108
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.972
82 million times over.

109
00:03:23.972 --> 00:03:26.767
Thank you, Drew, thank you so much.

110
00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.260
(audience applauding)

111
00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.260
Now, were the casting directors and everybody like excited

112
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.600
about "Derry Girls"?

113
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.830
Because everybody loves Derry Girls.

114
00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:37.993
And was that something-
Yeah.

115
00:03:37.993 --> 00:03:41.940
That they were excited by?
Look, there you are.

116
00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.510
Did they mention it?

117
00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.400
I'm always very fashionable in every role.

118
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.660
With Penelope, it's the yellow dresses,

119
00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.970
With Claire, it's a lot of headbands,

120
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.880
a lot of 90's regalia.

121
00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:55.270
Yeah, we just finished the final season of it, filming it.

122
00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.103
I know it's wild.

123
00:03:56.103 --> 00:03:58.620
It's just a really, really special show.

124
00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.970
It's about teenage girls growing up in Northern Ireland

125
00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.400
during the troubles.

126
00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.270
And yeah, it's just beautiful and heartfelt,

127
00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.240
but it had, you know, an endpoint

128
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.710
and I think there's something really special about a show

129
00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:12.010
that knows when the time is to exit the stage.

130
00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:12.843 line:15%
Yeah.

131
00:04:12.843 --> 00:04:15.385 line:15%
(upbeat music)

